Source: trindle-voice
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Build-Depends: cargo:native, rustc:native (>= 1.91)
Maintainer: Trindle <voice@trindle.org>
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://trindle.buildmorphic.com
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: trindle-voice
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, pipewire-bin
Description: on-device text to speech and speech server
 Reads text aloud with the Supertonic 2 voices, in pure Rust. The speech server
 starts on the first connection to its socket and leaves when idle.
 The speech models come from Hugging Face (Supertone/supertonic-2, revision
 75e6727618a02f323c720cba9478152d4bc16ca4) when the image is built. The voice files (about 253 MB) are installed in /usr/share/trindle-voice and
 stay under the BigScience Open RAIL-M License, whose use restrictions pass on.
